From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Brophy <professor_jonny@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 06:59:52 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] 9522: #9450: Add cspec-driven mechanism for fusing split
 call-argument pairs into one far pointer

9450: Add cspec-driven mechanism for fusing split
 call-arguments into one pointer

Adds a general, opt-in mechanism for fusing two adjacent stack
call-arguments (e.g. a page/bank byte and an offset word, each
pushed as independent immediates) into a single joined far-pointer
value at decompile time, driven by a new cspec schema element.

Addresses the case where two pieces of a far pointer are never
combined by any p-code operation visible in the caller -- only the
callee's own (opaque) calling convention associates them. This is
distinct from #817/#841, which cover far pointers already expressed
as a single CONCAT/ZEXT-shaped idiom within one instruction.

Two existing mechanisms were checked and confirmed unable to handle
this case:
- SegmentOp::unify() / ActionSegmentize only inspects a single
  CALLOTHER's own inputs, with no visibility into earlier
  instructions' p-code.
- ParamEntry::resolveJoin() requires each piece to already match an
  independently-existing ParamEntry elsewhere in the cspec model;
  a page-byte/offset-word pair with no independent meaning fails
  this and the cspec refuses to load.

fspec.hh / fspec.cc:
- New <farpointerjoin hislot="N" joinsize="N"/> element, decoded as
  a sibling of <returnsym> inside <prototype>. hislot is the 0-based
  index (matching pentry declaration order) of the more-significant
  piece; joinsize is the total byte size of the fused value, checked
  against the sum of the two adjacent pentry sizes at decode time.
- New FuncProto::FarPointerJoinSpec struct (public) and private
  farPointerJoins vector member, threaded through FuncProto::copy()
  (FuncCallSpecs::clone() inherits this via copy(), no separate edit
  needed).
- New public FuncProto::getFarPointerJoins() accessor.
- Not threaded through PrototypePieces / getPieces() / setPieces() --
  that struct has no join-spec field and is out of scope here.
- Known gap: FuncProto::encode() does not round-trip farPointerJoins
  (decode-only for now).

coreaction.hh / coreaction.cc:
- New ActionFarPointerJoin, modeled on ActionParamDouble::apply.
  Unlike ActionParamDouble (which requires prior dataflow evidence
  via SplitVarnode::inHandHi()/inHandLo()), this fires unconditionally
  on any call site whose bound FuncProto declares a
  <farpointerjoin>, since no such dataflow evidence exists for this
  case. Builds a SplitVarnode from the two input Varnodes, calls
  createJoinedWhole() to synthesize the merged Varnode (following
  the existing double.cc precedent for "no prior arithmetic joins
  these, just synthesize from fixed storage locations"), then folds
  it into the call via the existing
  checkInputJoin/opSetInput/opRemoveInput/doInputJoin sequence.
- Registered in ActionDatabase::universalAction immediately after
  ActionParamDouble("protorecovery") and before ActionSegmentize,
  so it runs while isInputActive() is still true.

Opt-in per prototype via cspec; architectures/prototypes that never
declare <farpointerjoin> see no behavior change.

Status: compiles clean (0 errors, no new warnings). Not yet exercised
end-to-end against a real binary/cspec -- no functional smoke test
has been run yet.

Add C++ unit test for farpointerjoin decode/encode round-trip

Adds funcproto_farpointerjoin_roundtrip to testfuncproto.cc, verifying
FuncProto::decode/encode correctly preserve <farpointerjoin> via the
built-in Toy architecture (no dependency on any out-of-tree processor
module). Also includes the compiler_spec.rxg schema addition and the
Java-side ElementId/AttributeId/PrototypeModel changes needed to
recognize <farpointerjoin> when a cspec is validated/loaded.

Fixes #9450
